%% Data flow for cobuilder-memory.
%% Level 2 = problem and solution. Flow a: the router sends a person prompt
%% to a quick run. Flow b: design stage 0 calls the moment tool, which starts
%% a deep run. Every step is a prediction that ADR-0039 carries.
sequenceDiagram
    actor Person
    participant Session as Claude Code session
    participant Design as architect design mode
    box transparent cobuilder-memory hooks module, proposed
    participant Writer as Note and receipt writer
    participant Queue as Queue and timer
    participant Router
    participant Quick as Quick run
    participant Moment as moment tool
    participant Guard as tool.call guard
    end
    participant Haiku as Haiku model
    participant Fork as Plan fork
    participant Agent as Deep run fork agent
    participant Hindsight as Hindsight MCP server

    rect rgba(120, 140, 93, 0.12)
    Note over Person,Hindsight: Flow a. The router sends a person prompt to a quick run.
    Person->>Session: Submits a prompt
    Session->>Queue: Prompt hook, for a person prompt in the main loop only, puts one job on the queue and returns at once
    Queue->>Router: Timer drains the queue and starts the router
    Router->>Haiku: $.model.complete with references/router.md, the last 1,500 characters, and the prompt
    Haiku-->>Router: {"read": "recall", "write": "none"}
    Router->>Quick: The recall label starts a quick run
    Quick->>Fork: $.model.fork with references/plan.md, the trigger, the labels, and the newest prompt
    Fork-->>Quick: JSON plan with six recall queries at most
    loop Each recall query in the plan
        Quick->>Hindsight: $.mcp.call recall, types world and experience, budget mid
        Hindsight-->>Quick: Results with memory ids and document ids
    end
    Quick->>Quick: Drops each result from this session's transcript and keeps 12 at most
    Quick->>Writer: Kept results
    Writer->>Session: $.session.append, one memory note in a hindsight_memories tag pair
    Writer->>Writer: Writes one receipt under .cobuilder-memory/runs/
    end

    rect rgba(106, 155, 204, 0.12)
    Note over Person,Hindsight: Flow b. Design stage 0 calls the moment tool, which starts a deep run.
    Design->>Moment: mcp__cobuilder-memory__moment with design-start, the name, the outcome, and the scope
    Moment->>Agent: $.agent.spawn, subagentType fork, references/deep-run.md and the moment input
    Moment-->>Design: run_id, kind deep, status started
    Note over Design: The tool returns at once. The memory note arrives later.
    Agent->>Guard: recall, with the fork's agent id
    Guard-->>Agent: Allowed. The tool is on the allow-list.
    Agent->>Hindsight: recall
    Hindsight-->>Agent: Memories with ids and dates
    Agent->>Guard: Read, with the fork's agent id
    Guard-->>Agent: Allowed. The tool is on the allow-list.
    Agent->>Agent: Reads the cited file and marks the claim
    opt A call outside the allow-list, such as Edit
        Agent->>Guard: Edit, with the fork's agent id
        Guard-->>Agent: Denied
    end
    Note over Guard,Agent: The spike tests that the guard sees each call of the fork.
    Agent-->>Writer: Checks JSON. Each claim is confirmed, contradicted, not applied, or cannot check.
    Note over Writer,Agent: Open fact: the module may have to append the fork's answer itself.
    Writer->>Session: $.session.append, one memory note
    Writer->>Writer: Writes one receipt with each tool call and its allowed flag
    end
